		summary = '**Ibn Rushd** (14 April 1126 – 11 December 1198), Latinized as **Averroes**, was an [[Al-Andalus|Andalusian]] polymath and jurist who was proficient in a variety of intellectual fields, including [[Philosophy|philosophy]], theology, medicine, [[Astronomy|astronomy]], [[Physics|physics]], [[Psychology|psychology]], [[Mathematics|mathematics]], neurology, Islamic jurisprudence, law, and [[Linguistics|linguistics]]. The author of more than 100 books and treatises, his philosophical works include numerous commentaries on [[Aristotle]], for which he was known in the [[Western world]] as "The Commentator" and "Father of Rationalism".',
