		summary = "**Cai Lun**, formerly romanized as **Ts'ai Lun**, was a Chinese eunuch court official of the Eastern Han dynasty. He occupies a pivotal place in the history of paper due to his addition of pulp via [[Bark (botany)|tree bark]] and hemp ends which resulted in the large-scale manufacture and worldwide spread of paper. Although traditionally regarded as the inventor of [[Paper|paper]], earlier forms of paper have existed since the 3rd century BCE, so Cai's contributions were an innovation, rather than an [[Invention|invention]].",
